# ============================================================================
# SearchLab - environment variables
# ============================================================================
#
# You do NOT need a `.env` file, locally or on Vercel.
#
# There is exactly ONE optional variable: VITE_ENGINE_URL
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNNING ON YOUR LAPTOP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Do nothing. With no `.env`, the frontend automatically targets the local
#   engine at http://127.0.0.1:8000.
#
#   Start the engine first:
#       python python_engine.py
#
#   -> Python AND Java both work locally.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNNING ON VERCEL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Do nothing. The engine is deployed in the SAME Vercel project (see
#   `vercel.json`, which defines two Vercel "Services": `web` and `engine`),
#   so the frontend calls its own origin automatically.
#
#   -> Python works. Java does NOT (Vercel ships no JDK), so the Java button
#      is hidden automatically after the frontend probes /health.
#
#   IMPORTANT: the project's Framework Preset must be set to `Services` in
#   Vercel (Settings -> Build and Deployment). A project builds as services
#   only when that preset is selected AND `vercel.json` has a `services` key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHEN WOULD I SET THIS AT ALL?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Only if the engine runs on a DIFFERENT host than the frontend, e.g.
#       VITE_ENGINE_URL=https://searchlab-engine.example.com
#
#   It is read at BUILD time, so changing it requires a rebuild/redeploy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * The `VITE_` prefix is required: Vite only exposes variables with it to
#   frontend code. Never put secrets in a VITE_ variable - they end up
#   readable in the shipped JavaScript.
#
# * This file is a template only. Vite does not read it. To use a real local
#   override, copy it to `.env` (which is git-ignored). You do not need one.
# ============================================================================

# Only set this if your engine is NOT co-located with the frontend:
# VITE_ENGINE_URL=https://searchlab-engine.example.com
